1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:01,430
It's Day 1 at a new job.

2
00:00:01,710 --> 00:00:05,723
The laptop isn't ready. Email doesn't work. The ID card isn't printed.

3
00:00:05,908 --> 00:00:07,991
Nobody knows why, not even the joiner.

4
00:00:08,455 --> 00:00:11,650
Five teams run onboarding. Nobody owns the whole chain.

5
00:00:11,813 --> 00:00:14,789
So one late item quietly breaks everything after it.

6
00:00:14,986 --> 00:00:17,367
The joiner finds out last: on Day 1.

7
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:21,169
Meet Navo: an AI agent that owns onboarding end to end.

8
00:00:21,235 --> 00:00:26,864
It tracks every dependency, acts before Day 1 breaks, and asks before anything sensitive.

9
00:00:27,164 --> 00:00:30,679
Anand joins Halden on Monday. Navo has read his documents; one is missing.

10
00:00:30,923 --> 00:00:33,621
He uploads a bill; Navo reads it and checks it against his ID.

11
00:00:34,022 --> 00:00:36,577
One unreadable date? It asks about that field only.

12
00:00:37,185 --> 00:00:41,477
Four days before Day 1, Navo's daily check runs. Every tool call shows live.

13
00:00:42,131 --> 00:00:44,955
The Employee ID is two days late. The laptop depends on it.

14
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:47,374
Risk: high. Zero days of slack.

15
00:00:47,863 --> 00:00:50,665
It checks its permissions, then reminds HR on its own.

16
00:00:51,123 --> 00:00:53,857
Anand gets one calm update. He chases no one.

17
00:00:54,065 --> 00:00:56,247
And every action shows its reason and policy.

18
00:00:56,547 --> 00:00:59,723
Priya in HR sees only exceptions, and what Navo already did.

19
00:00:59,923 --> 00:01:03,138
She issues the ID. Within a minute, Navo raises IT requests.

20
00:01:03,261 --> 00:01:05,176
On Anand's phone, the blocker is cleared.

21
00:01:05,571 --> 00:01:09,809
If HR never replies, Navo offers a loaner laptop at the last safe moment.

22
00:01:09,876 --> 00:01:12,423
That's an asset change, so Anand decides.

23
00:01:12,759 --> 00:01:16,549
Approved. Day 1 is covered, and HR Ops is escalated.

24
00:01:16,849 --> 00:01:21,875
Anand can ask anything. Navo answers from his live state and Halden's policies.

25
00:01:22,116 --> 00:01:24,173
It cites only the sections it retrieved.

26
00:01:24,486 --> 00:01:27,106
Ask in Hindi, and Navo answers in Hindi.

27
00:01:27,733 --> 00:01:31,623
HR adds a policy, and Navo splits it into sections it can cite.

28
00:01:31,932 --> 00:01:36,192
Once published, Ask Navo answers from it at once, citing the section.

29
00:01:36,404 --> 00:01:37,986
No retraining. No deploy.

30
00:01:38,402 --> 00:01:42,013
Priya also sees every joiner's Day 1, from the same rules Navo uses.

31
00:01:42,215 --> 00:01:43,815
What if IT takes a week longer?

32
00:01:44,043 --> 00:01:47,403
3 joiners at risk of a broken Day 1; IT drives all of them.

33
00:01:48,029 --> 00:01:51,369
Friday: everything's ready in one pickup. Day 1 runs to plan.

34
00:01:51,515 --> 00:01:54,588
Week 1 and Day 30 arrive with what he needs, on time.

35
00:01:55,025 --> 00:01:58,871
20 of 26 tasks closed in his first month. Only 6 needed Anand.

36
00:01:59,039 --> 00:02:01,476
Every one of its 148 tool calls is logged.

37
00:02:01,801 --> 00:02:06,178
Under the hood: Claude understands, and code decides: dates, risk and permissions.

38
00:02:06,505 --> 00:02:10,197
Each task gets the right-sized Claude model, and personal data is masked.

39
00:02:10,509 --> 00:02:12,633
The public demo runs offline, so it's free to try.

40
00:02:12,986 --> 00:02:16,109
Bring your own Claude key to watch it live. Navo never stores it.

41
00:02:16,409 --> 00:02:20,887
264 tests, a load test and an AI benchmark run on every push.

42
00:02:21,323 --> 00:02:23,100
About seven cents of Claude per joiner.

43
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:28,777
Next: replace the simulated HR and IT systems with real ones. Navo stays the same.

44
00:02:28,963 --> 00:02:31,307
Navo. AI that handles onboarding.
